cff-version: 1.2.0
title: STS-Prog — Sparse Temporal Selection with Progressive refinement
message: >-
  If you use STS-Prog in your research, please cite this repository
  as the canonical reference for the architecture.
authors:
  - given-names: "Geroin"
    family-names: "..."
    alias: "masterofnuggets313"
    email: "masterofnuggets313@users.noreply.github.com"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/masterofnuggets313/chaotic-llm"
repository-code: "https://github.com/masterofnuggets313/chaotic-llm"
abstract: >-
  STS-Prog is a language model architecture that replaces attention
  with content-based top-k key selection plus Pecora-Carroll chaotic
  synchronization. It achieves competitive PPL (19.2–24.5) and
  superior retrieval (47–50%) against parameter-matched transformers
  at 900K scale, with linear O(W·d·L) scaling and the ability to
  decode on 2M+ context windows on a 12GB GPU via Fracode-compressed
  state (24 bytes per position).
keywords:
  - chaotic neural networks
  - sparse attention
  - language model
  - Pecora-Carroll synchronization
  - product quantization
  - retrieval-augmented
